The code statements that lead to the bug are:
devl_param_driverinit_value_set(devlink, DEVLINK_PARAM_GENERIC_ID_ENABLE_PHC, value);
(inside ena_devlink_disable_phc_param and ena_devlink_configure_params, without holding the devlink lock)

Reason:
The function devl_param_driverinit_value_set() requires the devlink instance lock to be held (enforced by devl_assert_locked()). In the original code, this call was made without acquiring the lock, triggering the lock assertion warning during probe (ena_probe → ena_devlink_alloc → ena_devlink_configure_params or ena_devlink_disable_phc_param).

The code statements that fix the bug are:
+	devl_lock(devlink);
	devl_param_driverinit_value_set(devlink, DEVLINK_PARAM_GENERIC_ID_ENABLE_PHC, value);
+	devl_unlock(devlink);
(also the same lock/unlock pattern added to ena_devlink_configure_params)

Reason:
Adding devl_lock() before and devl_unlock() after the devl_param_driverinit_value_set() call ensures the required devlink lock is held, satisfying the lock assertion and preventing the warning.

